# Real ballot-level preference data for the 2002 Irish general election, Dublin West
# constituency (9 candidates, 3 seats, 29988 valid votes). Converted from the "soi" (strict
# orders, incomplete) format at https://www.preflib.org/dataset/00001 (PrefLib's "Irish
# Election Data", series 00001-00000002) -- originally posted by the Dublin County Returning
# Officer, since taken offline, and donated to PrefLib by Jeffrey O'Neill (OpenSTV.org).
#
# First preferences match Wikipedia's "Dublin West (Dail constituency)" page exactly: Lenihan
# 8086, Higgins 6442, Burton 3810, Terry 3694, McDonald 2404, Morrissey 2370, Doherty Ryan
# 2300, Bonnie 748, Smyth 134 (sums to 29988). Lenihan, Higgins, and Burton were the three TDs
# actually elected -- this file's expected replay (below) reproduces that same winner set
# exactly.
#
# IMPORTANT CAVEAT: see dublin_north_2002.blt's header for the full explanation -- this is a
# deterministic Droop+WIGM replay of the real ballot data, cross-validated stage-by-stage
# against jklundell/droop's independent implementation (matched exactly), not a replay of
# Ireland's own official count (which uses non-reproducible random-sample surplus transfers).
